sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 8-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite faithfully reproduces None. This is a cross-law synthesis / aggregator module. No organism, tissue, specimen image, experimental dataset or published figure is loaded or compared; Law 7's data come from the repository's own S_6 sorting simulation morphology" ;
        dcterms:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py, docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean, morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real None. This is a cross-law synthesis / aggregator module. No organism, tissue, specimen image, experimental dataset or published figure is loaded or compared; Law 7's data come from the repository's own S_6 sorting simulation specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json; output: media/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png; organism: None. This is a cross-law synthesis / aggregator module. No organism, tissue, specimen image, experimental dataset or published figure is loaded or compared; Law 7's data come from the repository's own S_6 sorting simulation; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, lean 4.35.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2020): voltage-gated gap-junction coupling G_ij(V_i, V_j) = G_0 / [(1 + e^{(V_i - V_th)/V_0})(1 + e^{(V_j - V_th)/V_0})] with polarising and depolarising channel currents; depolarised domains electrically isolate | Pietak & Levin (2016, 2017): Nernst-Planck electrodiffusion in BETSE; at zero flux the charged-morphogen ratio is Boltzmann, exp(-zF dV / RT), independent of gap-junction permeability | Chvykov et al. (2021): low-rattling principle P_ss ∝ exp(-gamma R) tested on smarticle collectives and simulation; the 'rattling' is a diffusion-tensor quantity, not a scalar exit rate | Watson & Szathmary (2016): natural induction / Hebbian deepening of visited attractors; Pigozzi, Goldstein & Levin (2025): associative conditioning in continuous GRN ODE models with measured conditioning success; Biswas et al. (2023): pathway-level memory in transcriptional network models | Hoel et al. (2013), Hoel (2026): causal emergence via effective information and the determinism/degeneracy decomposition CP = det - deg | Levin (2019, 2022): TAME cognitive light cone (diagrammatic); Bongard & Levin (2023): polycomputing (conceptual); Shreesha & Levin (2025): agent-based spatial Prisoner's Dilemma with controllable borders; reconstructed_in_script: Law 1 (L177-L225): N-cell linear diffusion-leak BVP -G (V_{i-1} - 2V_i + V_{i+1}) + (G_half/N) V_i = delta_{i0}; reach L = sum_i V_i / V_0 at G_gj in {0, 0.5, 1.0} and on a 51-point grid; continuum sqrt(1/k) tanh(N sqrt(k)); Hill curve 1 + (N-1) G/(G + G_half) computed but unused | Law 2 (L231-L277, unchanged since Pass 3): 20-cell ODE, cells 0-4 clamped at -10 mV, cubic bistable I_ion with roots -60 / -38 / -10 mV (not Cervera's channel currents), Bell-Boltzmann vs ohmic G_ij, RK45 to t = 80 | Law 3 (L283-L331): 1-D zero-flux BVP with central-difference / Pade(1,1) edge coefficients a_i = G(-1 + dv/2), b_{i+1} = G(1 + dv/2) on a linear voltage profile; grid refinement N_ap = 15..240 and a 5-value G_gj sweep at N_ap = 120 | Law 4 (L337-L404): 24-state CTMC, W(i->j) = r_i^gamma K_ij(alpha) with K(alpha) = (1 - alpha) K_sym + alpha K_trap, K_sym Sinkhorn-symmetrised doubly stochastic, K_trap row-normalised weights linspace(0.1, 2.5)^2.5 (column sums != 1); stationary vector from L^T p = 0; log-log fit of p against the fixed r_exit at alpha = 0, 0.5, 0.9 | Laws 5 and 7 (L410-L449): 4-row x 3-gate truth table; S_6 CE2 numbers read from the hash-pinned sorting-morphogenesis JSON | Law 6 (L455-L540): 16-gene symmetric J, Hebbian J += eta s s^T for 15 epochs, energy trace, basin fraction over 120 four-flip trials; 3-node ODE dx_CS = -x_CS + I_CS, dx_M = -0.02 x_M + 0.25 sigma(12 (x_CS x_US - 0.5)), dx_US = -x_US + sigma(12 (I_US + 0.9 x_M x_CS - 0.55)) in four phases (CS test, paired training t = 25, washout t = 5, CS test t = 10) | Law 8 (L546-L580, unchanged): pi_C(k) = (1 - k^-1/2) b - c and pi_D(k) = b k^-1/2 over k = 1..36; exact m x m directed bond count for m = 1..6 | 8 Lean theorems (Loop L30-L288, unchanged since Pass 3; duplicated in MathOfBiology.lean L1200-L1375), each on Nat/Int/Bool reductions of the law; transfer_boundary: The 8 laws are evaluated on synthetic parameter sets chosen by the builder (cubic current coefficients, r_exit table, K_trap weights, J ~ N(0, 0.25), 3-node ODE gains, b = 2, c = 1); no quantity is compared with a value measured in Cervera 2020, Pietak 2016/2017, Chvykov 2021, Pigozzi 2025 or Shreesha 2025 | Law 4's breakdown is now a genuine property of the model (non-doubly-stochastic routing with fixed exit rates), but K_trap is a builder construction and the magnitude of the breakdown is misreported in the criteria doc (+0.7618 vs the computed +0.1866) | Law 3's grid-refinement convergence is a genuine numerical check of the discretisation against the Boltzmann closed form; the G_gj invariance is still linear algebra (G_gj scales Q) | Law 1's BVP and its continuum closed form agree to 1.6 %; the Hill formula the law was previously scored on disagrees with the BVP by RMS 55 cells over the grid and is now neither the metric nor fitted, despite the docstring | Law 6's 3-node ODE is a hand-tuned minimal conditioning circuit, not a model from Pigozzi 2025 or Biswas 2023, and its docstring describes a different circuit with different results | Law 8's k >= 17 strict-dominance threshold applies 1 - 1/sqrt(k) to non-square k that no m x m cluster realises; the first exact square with strict dominance is k = 25; does_not_claim: This audit does not claim any of the 8 source equations is wrong as published, nor that any Lean theorem fails to check (all 8 compile with 0 sorry); it scores whether the suite implements, exercises and validates the laws and whether the O1/O2, T1-T4 and C1-C6 tags are earned by linked artefacts | It does not verify the content of the 63 cited videos (no transcripts offline) and does not recompute the S_6 TPM behind quantifying_emergence_ce2_metrics.json; it re-checks only the arithmetic consistency of the imported numbers | It does not score the 17 CHANNEL_CONCEPTS_INDEX items, which are correctly excluded from law status]; other sources: Extended Iterated, Spatialized Prisoner's Dilemma: Game Theory of Multicellularity with Agent-Controlled Borders <https://osf.io/kpzju_v2>, sorting-morphogenesis/figures/quantifying_emergence_ce2_metrics.json - S_n sorting Causal Emergence 2.0 metrics (n = 3..6) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib>, datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json - 374-video metadata index of @drmichaellevin <https://www.youtube.com/@drmichaellevin>" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.patter.2025.101472>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tree.2015.11.009>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/9781009300940>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jpclett.0c00641>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-025-08411-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1314922110>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1966.10502008>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2017.0425>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abc6182>,
            <https://doi.org/10.3389/fbioe.2016.00055>,
            <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201>,
            <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>,
            <https://doi.org/10.3390/biomimetics8010110>,
            <https://doi.org/10.3390/e25050748>,
            <https://doi.org/10.3390/e26040288>,
            <https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24010285> .

    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .

    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py" ;
